# Product version bumps

Product versioning is defined in `VERSIONING.md`. Follow that file; this rule only makes the bump step hard to skip.

## When finishing product work

If the change affects what a lifter sees or does (UI, logging, planning, account, shell upload), edit `evo-lift/app-version.json` in the **same** change before you finish.

| Part | When |
| --- | --- |
| Major | A lifter has to relearn an existing way of logging, planning, or managing an account. |
| Minor | A lifter gets a new capability, such as a new screen or a new way to log or plan. |
| Patch | A fix, a wording change, or a shell-only Play upload that does not add a capability. |

Bump only one step (for example `1.1.0` → `1.1.1`). Do not skip numbers. Do not put a `v` in the JSON file.

## When not to bump

Skip the bump for changes that are not a product release: Cursor rules, docs-only edits, tests-only, tooling, or internal refactors with no lifter-facing change.

## Do not

- Leave product work at the previous version.
- Hand-edit Android version codes; Gradle reads `app-version.json`.
- Treat `package.json` or OpenAPI versions as the product version.
